=== Prompt ===
Who is Donald Trump?

=== Response ===
Donald John Trump is an American businessman, real estate developer, and politician who served as the 45th President of the United States from January 20, 2017, to January 20, 2021. He was born on June 14, 1946, in Brooklyn, New York.

Before entering politics, Trump was known for his business ventures, particularly in real estate and television. He founded The Trump Organization, a real estate company that built and managed numerous high-profile properties around the world. He also appeared as a television personality, hosting the reality TV show "The Apprentice" from 2004 to 2015.

Trump ran for president as a member of the Republican Party in the 2016 election and won, defeating Democratic nominee Hillary Clinton. His campaign focused on issues such as economic policies, immigration, and foreign policy. As president, he implemented various policies and executive orders, often emphasizing a "America First" approach.

Trump's presidency was marked by several controversies and significant changes in U.S. domestic and international policies. After losing the 2020 presidential election to Joe Biden, he has continued to be involved in public life and remains a prominent figure in American politics.

